+// FZY: SDP user-copy bookend. Marks a kernel user-copy primitive
+// (e.g. copy_from_user / copy_to_user) whose buffer argument should be
+// routed through an untyped staging alloca by clang at each call site
+// where the buffer's pointee is a sensitive type with a constant size
+// matching sizeof(*pointee). After the call, clang emits a kernel-only
+// typed copy between staging and the original typed buffer, so tagged
+// fields end up written via sd_tag1 / read via ld_tag1 even though the
+// underlying user-copy assembly only deals in plain sd/ld.
+//
+// `BufIdx` is the kernel-side buffer argument; `SizeIdx` is the size
+// (in bytes). Both are 1-based parameter indices.
